.DS_Store
node_modules/
*.log
.claude/worktrees/

# Spec and tickets are working documents, kept local rather than versioned.
# They stay on disk and are still the contract -- see CLAUDE.md / the /spec and
# /tickets skills -- they are just not tracked here.
SPEC_*.md
TICKETS_*.md

# The design record stays local too, by decision 2026-07-30. It is what the
# source comments mean by "see DESIGN.md": the reasoning, the rejected
# alternatives and the slice logs, promoted out of the two specs before they were
# deleted. Accepted consequence: the published tree carries references to a file
# it does not ship. `git add -f DESIGN.md` is the whole reversal.
DESIGN.md

# The internal audit reports stay local too. The security record ships as
# SECURITY.md (current posture) and CHANGELOG.md (found and fixed per release);
# see SECURITY.md "How this record is kept". Publishing a per-commit adversarial
# audit of a pre-release codebase would mean maintaining a second, staler
# security narrative beside the one a reader actually needs.
findings/

# CONTEXT.md is working vocabulary for this repo's own sessions, not documentation
# for someone who cloned it. Same reasoning as the specs above: it describes decisions
# still in motion, so publishing it means maintaining a second, vaguer account of the
# project beside README.md.
CONTEXT.md
